      "description": "True rollers — stocky, crow-sized birds with brilliant blue-and-turquoise plumage, named for their spectacular aerial courtship displays in which they tumble and roll through the air. They are among the most colourful birds of the Old World, found in open country across Europe, Africa, and Asia.",
